1
00:00:00,470 --> 00:00:01,840
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:03,340
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:09,280
- Ms. Kang Da Mi?
- Hello, Team Leader Cha.

4
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:27,300
Are you okay, Da Mi?
Are you hurt anywhere?

5
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:30,870
I am fine, but your arm...

6
00:00:31,670 --> 00:00:32,770
I am fine, too.

7
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:36,110
(Episode 32)

8
00:00:36,170 --> 00:00:37,180
Wait a second.

9
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:40,040
Try to get up slowly.

10
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:52,460
I am sorry. I was trying to carry
so many things all at once.

11
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:57,800
No, it is fine.
By the way, what brings you here?

12
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:01,730
I started working today...

13
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:03,640
as Head Designer
Cha Seung Yun's assistant.

14
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:06,640
Seung Yun... I mean,

15
00:01:07,070 --> 00:01:09,340
Head Designer
Cha Seung Yun's assistant?

16
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:12,580
Then why did you reject my offer...

17
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:14,210
so flatly?

18
00:01:15,010 --> 00:01:16,450
I feel a little hurt.

19
00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:20,520
Strictly speaking,

20
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:22,750
I do not belong
to Hwanggeum Apparel.

21
00:01:22,820 --> 00:01:24,590
Team Leader Cha?

22
00:01:28,490 --> 00:01:30,130
Hello, CEO Jeon.

23
00:01:31,630 --> 00:01:32,730
What is going on here?

24
00:01:33,570 --> 00:01:36,630
What business does Manager Kang
have at our company?

25
00:01:37,170 --> 00:01:38,300
Well, you see...

26
00:01:38,540 --> 00:01:40,570
She said she started
working today...

27
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,410
as Head Designer Cha Seung Yun's
assistant, CEO Jeon.

28
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:44,580
No way.

29
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:47,050
What qualifications does
a department store clerk have?

30
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:50,080
I received an offer directly
from the head designer,

31
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:51,450
and that is why I came to work here.

32
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:53,520
From Designer Jaden Cha?

33
00:01:55,420 --> 00:01:56,420
How interesting.

34
00:01:57,490 --> 00:01:59,090
Did you know about this,
Team Leader Cha?

35
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:01,130
No. I just heard about it myself.

36
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:03,930
This is my first time
working as an assistant,

37
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,630
but I majored in design in college.

38
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:09,370
- I will work hard to learn...
- A company is not a school.

39
00:02:10,030 --> 00:02:11,570
It is a place you join
after you learn.

40
00:02:14,110 --> 00:02:16,810
CEO Jeon, as for Da Mi's portfolio,

41
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:18,410
Head Designer
Cha Seung Yun directly...

42
00:02:18,440 --> 00:02:20,510
I can look into that myself.

43
00:02:21,250 --> 00:02:23,780
Kang Da Mi, go back
to what you were doing.

44
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:26,080
Shouldn't you go inside...

45
00:02:26,150 --> 00:02:27,550
and get back to work,
Team Leader Cha?

46
00:02:27,990 --> 00:02:30,460
Yes, I was on my way down
to the lobby...

47
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:31,760
because a guest had arrived.

48
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:33,460
Give that to me, Team Leader Cha.

49
00:02:34,090 --> 00:02:35,460
Let's go. I'll help you carry them.

50
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:40,300
I told you to dump those magazines.

51
00:02:40,370 --> 00:02:41,900
What are you still doing out here?

52
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:44,640
CEO Jeon.

53
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:47,440
This is Ms. Kang Da Mi,
who will be working with me.

54
00:02:48,210 --> 00:02:49,410
You two have met before, right?

55
00:02:50,110 --> 00:02:51,810
Designer Jaden Cha.

56
00:02:52,710 --> 00:02:55,310
I would appreciate an explanation.

57
00:02:56,010 --> 00:02:57,020
What exactly...

58
00:02:58,420 --> 00:02:59,420
About Ms. Kang Da Mi?

59
00:03:00,690 --> 00:03:03,190
I told you before that I would hire
my own team members.

60
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:05,160
I chose to hire her myself.

61
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:09,460
She has only ever worked
in retail, so...

62
00:03:09,790 --> 00:03:11,530
Truthfully, I have my concerns.

63
00:03:13,930 --> 00:03:16,830
She is my assistant.
Since we decided to work together,

64
00:03:16,940 --> 00:03:18,000
I will take full responsibility
for her.

65
00:03:19,070 --> 00:03:21,510
Responsibility?

66
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:23,140
Yes, responsibility.

67
00:03:25,510 --> 00:03:28,010
CEO Jeon, I have quite a bit of work
piled up at the moment.

68
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:29,280
So we will take our leave.

69
00:03:30,820 --> 00:03:31,820
Give me that.

70
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:38,060
Looks like we will be seeing
each other often.

71
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:39,520
Yes.

72
00:03:44,330 --> 00:03:46,400
I will head downstairs
as well, CEO Jeon.

73
00:03:52,770 --> 00:03:54,070
She is certainly resourceful.

74
00:03:55,010 --> 00:03:58,440
How did the head designer
even know Manager Kang and hire her?

75
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:01,280
Should I look into it separately?

76
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:04,850
Yes, look into it.

77
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:08,150
I don't have a good feeling
about this.

78
00:04:08,620 --> 00:04:11,120
Understood. I will check right away
and report back.

79
00:04:15,230 --> 00:04:16,560
Hurry up and get over here.

80
00:04:20,730 --> 00:04:22,470
First you covered my mouth
this morning,

81
00:04:22,530 --> 00:04:24,270
and now you are grabbing my arm?

82
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:28,110
I was just in a huge rush.

83
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:29,570
I am sorry.
I will be careful from now on.

84
00:04:30,710 --> 00:04:33,980
By the way, you said you are
Assistant Manager Cha Se Na, right?

85
00:04:35,010 --> 00:04:37,850
Why are you being so persistent
like a stalker? Seriously.

86
00:04:38,550 --> 00:04:39,650
As an assistant manager,

87
00:04:39,650 --> 00:04:41,590
surely you have other duties
to handle.

88
00:04:41,950 --> 00:04:43,390
I really do not get it.

89
00:04:43,450 --> 00:04:45,320
Am I the only debtor
assigned to you?

90
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:47,560
How did you know?

91
00:04:48,390 --> 00:04:50,190
You really can tell
you went to a top university.

92
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:52,100
Your brain works on another level.

93
00:04:52,400 --> 00:04:55,770
Still, how on earth did you manage
to end up in so much debt?

94
00:04:55,970 --> 00:04:57,640
You seem like
a remarkably sharp man.

95
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:59,400
I just cannot wrap
my head around it.

96
00:04:59,870 --> 00:05:01,140
Why do you need to know that?

97
00:05:01,870 --> 00:05:03,980
Do I really have to
satisfy your curiosity?

98
00:05:04,180 --> 00:05:05,680
Am I not allowed to just ask?

99
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:07,250
We might be seeing each other
for a long time.

100
00:05:07,450 --> 00:05:08,810
Do not be so prickly.

101
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:10,920
Who said we would keep seeing
each other?

102
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:15,950
I will transfer some
overdue interest right now. Happy?

103
00:05:16,650 --> 00:05:18,260
Please, just go.

104
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:20,660
Do you actually have
the money for that, sir?

105
00:05:22,930 --> 00:05:25,030
I honestly thought
it would take you much longer,

106
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:26,630
so if you show good faith
by paying even a little,

107
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:28,300
I would be very grateful.

108
00:05:32,670 --> 00:05:34,240
There. Satisfied?

109
00:05:34,710 --> 00:05:38,340
Yes. Since you made a payment,
we can part ways here for today.

110
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:42,380
And since you hate it so much
when I drop by your place,

111
00:05:42,450 --> 00:05:44,880
let us make sure to meet
right here from now on, sir.

112
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:48,290
After you send over your
repayment plan first, of course.

113
00:05:48,590 --> 00:05:49,620
Bye.

114
00:05:55,290 --> 00:05:56,960
Is she completely out of her mind?

115
00:05:58,100 --> 00:05:59,100
Fine.

116
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:00,830
I will put together
that repayment plan...

117
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:02,070
and send it to you no matter what.

118
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:04,300
I hope I never have
to see you again.

119
00:06:07,170 --> 00:06:09,870
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

120
00:06:22,950 --> 00:06:24,260
What is wrong, Mi Mi?

121
00:06:26,460 --> 00:06:28,990
It is nothing. Just my stomach.

122
00:06:47,980 --> 00:06:51,220
What did you eat behind our backs
that your stomach is upset?

123
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:55,250
Why don't we go see
Dr. Ju for a checkup?

124
00:06:55,550 --> 00:06:57,620
It seems like the medicine
is not doing anything at all.

125
00:06:58,020 --> 00:07:00,360
I just took it a little while ago.
How can it kick in already?

126
00:07:01,290 --> 00:07:03,590
I forgot to take it this morning.

127
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:06,360
Come on, Mom.

128
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:10,330
How can you forget
to take your prescribed medication?

129
00:07:12,370 --> 00:07:15,270
You can't even wipe a table right.
Give me that.

130
00:07:16,510 --> 00:07:17,910
Can't you see it's sticky?

131
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:21,350
Aunt Ri Ja said Grandma stepped out
without saying a word,

132
00:07:21,410 --> 00:07:24,150
so I came out to help.
Why are you picking on me?

133
00:07:24,980 --> 00:07:26,520
You don't appreciate
that your eldest son...

134
00:07:26,620 --> 00:07:27,620
is worried about you.

135
00:07:29,950 --> 00:07:32,920
If you're going to help,
at least do it right.

136
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:03,860
(Ultra Pain Relief Patch)

137
00:08:07,590 --> 00:08:09,630
Why does my body feel so heavy?

138
00:08:11,260 --> 00:08:13,060
I used to feel refreshed...

139
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:14,970
after passing out
and sleeping deeply.

140
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:19,000
I guess you can't fool age.

141
00:09:01,510 --> 00:09:03,110
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

142
00:09:03,210 --> 00:09:05,920
I'm going to take a walk
around the neighborhood.

143
00:09:07,250 --> 00:09:08,420
If there's anything Gang Nam can do,

144
00:09:08,450 --> 00:09:09,720
put him to work
while you get things done.

145
00:09:11,820 --> 00:09:12,820
I need to digest my food...

146
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:14,630
so I can prepare
for the dinner rush.

147
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:20,030
Come on, wouldn't it be better
to get examined one more time?

148
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:21,870
I already took my medicine.

149
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:23,400
I'll be right back.

150
00:09:29,910 --> 00:09:31,210
Hey, what are you doing?

151
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:34,550
Take this and soak it
in the kitchen sink.

152
00:09:35,380 --> 00:09:36,680
Got it.

153
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:38,520
Just soak it, right?

154
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:45,890
With all three of her kids
taking turns driving her crazy,

155
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:48,960
it'd be a miracle
if she didn't get sick.

156
00:09:50,390 --> 00:09:51,400
By the way,

157
00:09:51,530 --> 00:09:54,670
where has Mrs. Choi gone?
Why hasn't she come back?

158
00:09:56,730 --> 00:09:58,770
Wait, Se Na, you went by yourself...

159
00:09:59,270 --> 00:10:01,440
and actually collected
this much money again?

160
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:03,040
Dad,

161
00:10:03,310 --> 00:10:06,640
have I ever lied to you,
Mom, or Grandma?

162
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:10,250
If you don't believe me,
call the company and ask yourself.

163
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:15,050
So you went to inform him
of the repayment plan,

164
00:10:15,450 --> 00:10:19,860
and he paid you 5,000 dollars
on the spot for overdue interest?

165
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:22,260
- That's what I said, Grandma.
- I see.

166
00:10:22,330 --> 00:10:24,130
Anyway, Grandma,
I'm doing a great job...

167
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:28,270
- at work, right?
- Well, it is quite impressive.

168
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:30,330
It really is, Mother.

169
00:10:31,770 --> 00:10:32,770
Se Na,

170
00:10:33,070 --> 00:10:35,210
you can't just barge in
and threaten people...

171
00:10:35,270 --> 00:10:36,940
or disrupt their
daily lives and work.

172
00:10:37,010 --> 00:10:39,880
- You shouldn't do that.
- Come on, Dad.

173
00:10:40,110 --> 00:10:43,050
I only went there
because I had good reason to.

174
00:10:43,350 --> 00:10:46,020
Besides, your daughter
is as polite as can be.

175
00:10:48,220 --> 00:10:51,320
Grandma, since I'm
your granddaughter,

176
00:10:51,490 --> 00:10:54,090
I think I have
a natural talent for this.

177
00:10:54,090 --> 00:10:55,090
Don't you agree?

178
00:10:55,090 --> 00:10:59,230
Don't get carried away over
two months of overdue interest.

179
00:10:59,830 --> 00:11:03,830
Figure out how you are going to get
the principal back.

180
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:05,500
Yes, Grandma.

181
00:11:05,770 --> 00:11:08,440
What did you say
the debtor's name was?

182
00:11:08,610 --> 00:11:11,580
Dae Chi. Kang Dae Chi.

183
00:11:12,210 --> 00:11:13,710
What is the matter, Mother?

184
00:11:14,050 --> 00:11:17,110
I am just curious
what kind of person he is.

185
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:19,950
It is not like
I am pressed for time.

186
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:24,720
Kang Dae Chi.

187
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:26,960
I see.

188
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:39,840
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

189
00:11:39,940 --> 00:11:42,610
Why do I feel so nauseous?

190
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:44,980
It just will not settle down.

191
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:48,980
Should I walk around the block
one more time?

192
00:11:54,120 --> 00:11:56,190
Did Dr. Ju throw those out?

193
00:12:06,130 --> 00:12:09,330
This is a play script collection
I have really wanted to read.

194
00:12:10,630 --> 00:12:12,000
Is he really throwing it away?

195
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:20,110
Ma'am.

196
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:22,980
Oh, I am sorry. Did I startle you?

197
00:12:24,010 --> 00:12:25,580
I was on my way into my restaurant,

198
00:12:25,650 --> 00:12:27,450
and this script collection
caught my eye.

199
00:12:28,050 --> 00:12:31,420
I was just stopping by to ask
if you were throwing it out.

200
00:12:31,520 --> 00:12:34,090
I came out to check whether...

201
00:12:34,430 --> 00:12:38,130
our nursing assistant was
throwing out one of my prized books.

202
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:41,400
By the way,
are you into theater, too?

203
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:43,300
Yes.

204
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:46,100
I read a lot when I was younger,

205
00:12:46,340 --> 00:12:47,610
and because I dreamed
of being an actress,

206
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:49,170
I read so many play scripts.

207
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:53,010
This was one of my favorites,

208
00:12:53,910 --> 00:12:55,380
but because it is so old,

209
00:12:55,450 --> 00:12:57,280
it went out of print
and I could never find it.

210
00:12:57,980 --> 00:13:00,380
Yes, it must be hard
to find these days.

211
00:13:00,450 --> 00:13:01,720
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

212
00:13:01,790 --> 00:13:03,950
- Here.
- Thank you.

213
00:13:04,620 --> 00:13:06,160
A junior colleague in theater...

214
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:08,990
invited me
and gave me these tickets,

215
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:13,500
- and I had left them in here.
- I am so glad you found them.

216
00:13:14,530 --> 00:13:15,530
Well, then...

217
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:17,200
Excuse me.

218
00:13:18,340 --> 00:13:19,340
Yes?

219
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:22,070
There are two tickets for the play,

220
00:13:22,340 --> 00:13:25,710
and I was hoping
I could find someone to go with.

221
00:13:26,410 --> 00:13:28,350
Would you like to come with me?

222
00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:30,580
With me?

223
00:13:32,020 --> 00:13:34,590
Yes, if you do not mind.

224
00:13:35,020 --> 00:13:37,050
You said you dreamed
of being a theater actress.

225
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:40,060
Oh, that was a long time ago.

226
00:13:40,620 --> 00:13:42,760
A restaurant owner
has to look after her shop.

227
00:13:43,590 --> 00:13:45,600
Thank you for the offer, though.

228
00:13:45,660 --> 00:13:47,100
(Dr. Ju Kyung Ho)

229
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:49,400
Are you taking
your medication properly?

230
00:13:49,770 --> 00:13:51,600
You still look a bit pale.

231
00:13:52,770 --> 00:13:54,970
I was so busy that I forgot,

232
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:56,610
but I took it
just a little while ago.

233
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:58,110
I am sure it will get better.

234
00:13:58,610 --> 00:14:00,640
You must be busy,
so please head inside.

235
00:14:00,710 --> 00:14:02,080
If it does not improve,

236
00:14:02,210 --> 00:14:04,650
please be sure to stop by
the clinic anytime.

237
00:14:05,550 --> 00:14:06,880
Yes, I will.

238
00:14:08,920 --> 00:14:10,920
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

239
00:14:15,230 --> 00:14:17,830
Gosh, when was the last time
I saw a play?

240
00:14:21,170 --> 00:14:22,670
I should walk around the block
one more time...

241
00:14:23,430 --> 00:14:24,700
and get ready
to open the restaurant.

242
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:27,270
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

243
00:14:35,280 --> 00:14:39,080
Mom, you always hold on
to every single container.

244
00:14:39,620 --> 00:14:40,750
I enjoyed the food,

245
00:14:40,820 --> 00:14:42,550
and I washed
the container thoroughly.

246
00:14:42,620 --> 00:14:43,720
Here, take it.

247
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:46,560
You washed the container yourself?

248
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:51,000
- What was that woman doing?
- You know she works too.

249
00:14:51,860 --> 00:14:53,500
What does it matter who does it?

250
00:14:54,870 --> 00:14:57,170
Look at you living the high life.

251
00:14:58,370 --> 00:15:01,440
I told you to get out of town
before the kids' mom finds out.

252
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:03,510
Are you using this as an excuse
to keep me here?

253
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:05,610
Did you put the house on the market?

254
00:15:06,810 --> 00:15:08,450
We barely moved in.

255
00:15:08,510 --> 00:15:10,410
Where are we supposed
to go right now?

256
00:15:10,610 --> 00:15:12,580
Honestly, it is tough right now.

257
00:15:12,780 --> 00:15:15,390
Even though it is a basement
apartment, we are renting monthly.

258
00:15:15,650 --> 00:15:17,390
I really have nothing to my name.

259
00:15:18,390 --> 00:15:20,820
Once I save up some money...

260
00:15:24,530 --> 00:15:26,000
When you abandoned
your wife and kids...

261
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,030
to set up a second family,

262
00:15:27,030 --> 00:15:29,600
did you not know you would end up
in such a pitiful state today?

263
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:33,970
I knew all along
you would end up like this.

264
00:15:34,470 --> 00:15:36,840
I do not care
whether you have money or not,

265
00:15:37,310 --> 00:15:39,310
so stay out of their mom's sight
and get out quickly.

266
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:41,380
That will be good for you.

267
00:15:43,050 --> 00:15:45,550
You sound harsh,

268
00:15:45,620 --> 00:15:50,550
but I know your heart aches
for your only son.

269
00:15:51,620 --> 00:15:53,160
Who?

270
00:15:54,060 --> 00:15:55,060
Me?

271
00:15:55,930 --> 00:15:57,230
You crazy fool.

272
00:15:58,200 --> 00:15:59,500
Mom.

273
00:16:01,370 --> 00:16:02,470
Mom.

274
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:05,740
That "Grandma Oh" was
actually that jerk Kang Hak Sung?

275
00:16:08,570 --> 00:16:09,870
I cannot believe this.

276
00:16:12,210 --> 00:16:15,050
Mom, your skin is still so nice.

277
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:18,080
Mom, I am sorry.

278
00:16:21,290 --> 00:16:23,020
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

279
00:16:23,090 --> 00:16:26,290
- Let go, that hurts.
- It hurts?

280
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:28,530
Now you know what pain feels like?

281
00:16:28,730 --> 00:16:31,600
Wrecking our family wasn't enough...

282
00:16:31,800 --> 00:16:34,300
how long have you been working here?
Since when?

283
00:16:34,530 --> 00:16:36,600
Seeing my sister's restaurant
every time you walked by,

284
00:16:36,670 --> 00:16:38,070
did you feel no shame at all?

285
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:42,170
- You're in serious trouble now.
- Aunt.

286
00:16:42,240 --> 00:16:44,380
Let go of her first and talk.

287
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:46,340
What if customers see this,
seriously.

288
00:16:46,410 --> 00:16:48,380
Hey. Do you think customers
matter right now?

289
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:49,910
Did you forget
that your dad walked out...

290
00:16:49,980 --> 00:16:53,350
- because this woman seduced him?
- I never seduced him.

291
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:56,290
I just asked him to help us survive
now that we had a child.

292
00:16:56,350 --> 00:16:59,160
Hak Sung was the one
who chose me and our daughter.

293
00:16:59,220 --> 00:17:01,630
What? You have some nerve
to run your mouth.

294
00:17:01,730 --> 00:17:05,200
You should never have shown
your face to me.

295
00:17:05,330 --> 00:17:06,760
Just talk, let us talk.
Please, let go.

296
00:17:06,830 --> 00:17:07,830
I...

297
00:17:08,370 --> 00:17:11,440
- Ri Ja.
- Do you know who this is?

298
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:13,400
It is Park Ji Young.
She is the one...

299
00:17:13,470 --> 00:17:17,440
- who stabbed you in the back.
- Yes, I know. But first,

300
00:17:17,510 --> 00:17:19,280
let go of her hair.

301
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:22,250
- Please help me.
- Look at her.

302
00:17:22,610 --> 00:17:24,450
Ma'am, please stop her.

303
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:28,290
- She'll beat me to death!
- Who are you calling 'sister'?

304
00:17:28,350 --> 00:17:30,550
- Have you lost your mind?
- Jo Ri Ja.

305
00:17:31,050 --> 00:17:32,120
I said stop it.

306
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:40,630
Go inside the restaurant.

307
00:17:41,870 --> 00:17:42,870
Me?

308
00:17:43,830 --> 00:17:44,840
Yes.

309
00:17:46,670 --> 00:17:47,740
You too, Ri Ja.

310
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:51,440
Unbelievable.

311
00:17:51,980 --> 00:17:53,210
You little!

312
00:17:55,810 --> 00:17:57,820
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

313
00:17:58,680 --> 00:18:01,450
What on earth is going on?

314
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:06,590
Why did that woman suddenly show up?

315
00:18:11,360 --> 00:18:13,800
What about me? What should I do?
Should I go in or not?

316
00:18:13,860 --> 00:18:15,470
This is driving me crazy.

317
00:18:17,970 --> 00:18:20,640
You know you should never
show your face to me, right?

318
00:18:21,670 --> 00:18:22,910
I tried so hard to avoid running...

319
00:18:23,740 --> 00:18:28,110
into you, Mi Mi. I mean ma'am...
I really did all this time.

320
00:18:28,710 --> 00:18:31,520
Mona Ri Ja barged into
the clinic out of nowhere.

321
00:18:31,580 --> 00:18:32,980
I was terrified too.

322
00:18:33,380 --> 00:18:36,390
Hey. Stop calling her "Mi Mi."

323
00:18:36,690 --> 00:18:37,890
My sister gave you a room
to sleep in,

324
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:42,130
fed you when you had nowhere to go,
and paid you good money.

325
00:18:42,130 --> 00:18:43,790
And you repaid her with betrayal.

326
00:18:44,460 --> 00:18:45,560
Listen, Mi Mi.

327
00:18:45,930 --> 00:18:48,800
She got a job right down the street
at Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine,

328
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:52,640
and she has been commuting through
this alley every day, ducking you.

329
00:18:53,870 --> 00:18:55,040
Why here, of all places?

330
00:18:56,010 --> 00:18:57,140
Aren't you supposed to be living...

331
00:18:57,210 --> 00:18:58,410
in the Philippines
with Kang Hak Sung?

332
00:18:59,240 --> 00:19:01,010
How dare you show your face where...

333
00:19:01,080 --> 00:19:02,180
my family lives
and even get a job here?

334
00:19:02,810 --> 00:19:04,520
Do you have no shame?

335
00:19:05,380 --> 00:19:06,450
Well,

336
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:08,920
I still have to make a living.

337
00:19:10,620 --> 00:19:13,420
Our business went under completely,
and we are flat broke now.

338
00:19:14,290 --> 00:19:17,260
He said he found a place
within what little money he had,

339
00:19:17,330 --> 00:19:19,500
and it was in this neighborhood.
What was I supposed to do?

340
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,770
How did the great Kang Hak Sung
end up broke?

341
00:19:23,970 --> 00:19:25,170
Serves him right, though.

342
00:19:25,470 --> 00:19:27,240
He doesn't take after his mother.

343
00:19:27,740 --> 00:19:31,070
He is too gullible
and has always lived his life...

344
00:19:31,140 --> 00:19:32,710
just trying to please everyone.

345
00:19:33,310 --> 00:19:35,180
He quit his job to partner
with someone he trusted,

346
00:19:35,250 --> 00:19:37,180
and they expanded the business
too fast over there.

347
00:19:38,050 --> 00:19:41,520
Then his partner ran off,
leaving him with all the debt.

348
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:43,750
We barely settled things
and came back.

349
00:19:44,390 --> 00:19:45,890
You are actually the lucky one.

350
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:48,390
You do not have to live your life
supporting such a useless man.

351
00:19:48,990 --> 00:19:50,990
What? Who do you think
you are talking to?

352
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:53,800
That incompetent man.

353
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:55,830
You showed up and took him away.

354
00:19:56,500 --> 00:19:59,370
You came with a little kid
and clung to Kang Hak Sung,

355
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:01,270
crying that you had no way
to survive...

356
00:20:01,510 --> 00:20:02,810
and begging him
to take responsibility.

357
00:20:03,940 --> 00:20:07,240
Whether he is penniless or not,
I could not care less.

358
00:20:07,340 --> 00:20:09,950
I have no reason
to listen to your sob story.

359
00:20:11,210 --> 00:20:13,780
I am barely hanging on,
just living for my daughter...

360
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:14,920
Please...

361
00:20:15,220 --> 00:20:16,350
I mean, ma'am.

362
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:18,490
(Nursing Assistant Park Ji Young)

363
00:20:18,560 --> 00:20:20,990
I know I was in the wrong back then.

364
00:20:22,430 --> 00:20:25,560
I was just so lost,
trying to survive...

365
00:20:25,630 --> 00:20:28,070
while raising a child on my own.

366
00:20:28,400 --> 00:20:30,600
Even the place we moved into now
is a semi-basement.

367
00:20:30,670 --> 00:20:33,940
My life has truly hit rock bottom.
I am on the verge of breaking down.

368
00:20:35,410 --> 00:20:36,410
And?

369
00:20:38,140 --> 00:20:41,180
Could you please pretend...

370
00:20:41,410 --> 00:20:43,150
you don't know me
in front of Dr. Ju?

371
00:20:43,650 --> 00:20:45,550
At my age,
finding a job like this is rare,

372
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:47,020
and he was the one
who gave me a chance.

373
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:49,050
I'm genuinely grateful to him.

374
00:20:50,420 --> 00:20:53,420
I actually intended to quit today,

375
00:20:54,560 --> 00:20:55,730
but if I leave,

376
00:20:55,790 --> 00:20:57,190
I will not have a single penny
to my name,

377
00:20:57,430 --> 00:20:58,930
so I hesitated.

378
00:21:00,830 --> 00:21:02,070
Serves you right.

379
00:21:02,670 --> 00:21:03,730
By the way, Mi Mi,

380
00:21:04,130 --> 00:21:06,870
do we really have to stand here
and keep listening to her?

381
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:11,270
You have already
raised your kids well, haven't you?

382
00:21:11,340 --> 00:21:14,210
You have a home
and a great restaurant like this.

383
00:21:14,610 --> 00:21:16,010
For my daughter's sake,

384
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:18,550
I have to get us
out of that basement.

385
00:21:19,920 --> 00:21:21,990
Please, have some mercy.

386
00:21:22,390 --> 00:21:24,760
I will stay out of your sight
as much as I can, okay?

387
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:28,960
Get out.

388
00:21:29,890 --> 00:21:31,130
Mi Mi, please.

389
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:34,230
Get out of my restaurant.

390
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:36,230
I have to open for business.

391
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:48,180
Mi Mi.

392
00:21:48,610 --> 00:21:50,150
Are you really just going to
let her leave like this?

393
00:21:50,510 --> 00:21:51,620
Aren't you furious?

394
00:21:51,780 --> 00:21:53,620
You should have at least
slapped her in the face.

395
00:21:54,890 --> 00:21:56,190
Aren't we opening for dinner?

396
00:21:56,850 --> 00:21:58,520
How can you worry about business
after all that drama?

397
00:21:58,590 --> 00:22:01,190
Yes. Business comes first for me.

398
00:22:01,790 --> 00:22:03,090
I am the owner here.

399
00:22:04,530 --> 00:22:06,530
I am going to stop by the house
for a moment,

400
00:22:06,900 --> 00:22:09,030
so keep quiet and hurry up
with the prep work.

401
00:22:10,800 --> 00:22:13,170
How can you be so calm?

402
00:22:13,440 --> 00:22:15,710
Or are you so stunned
that you lost your mind?

403
00:22:16,610 --> 00:22:17,640
Unbelievable.

404
00:22:18,280 --> 00:22:21,110
What a wretched woman.
How dare she show her face here?

405
00:22:21,710 --> 00:22:22,780
It makes my blood boil.

406
00:22:46,270 --> 00:22:50,240
So that time
when he came by the restaurant...

407
00:22:51,370 --> 00:22:53,040
Did he show up
because he moved back here?

408
00:22:55,880 --> 00:22:58,320
How long has Mother
known about this?

409
00:23:01,250 --> 00:23:02,390
Even so...

410
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:07,320
Knowing everything I went through,
how could she...

411
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,900
Where have you been?

412
00:23:19,470 --> 00:23:23,440
I just had some errands to run.

413
00:23:24,880 --> 00:23:26,240
Aren't you getting ready to open?

414
00:23:27,310 --> 00:23:30,080
Why are you sitting here
doing nothing?

415
00:23:30,350 --> 00:23:32,250
My stomach is a bit upset.

416
00:23:32,750 --> 00:23:35,790
I was just getting some fresh air
before heading back inside.

417
00:23:37,590 --> 00:23:40,720
Did you go see Grandma Oh?

418
00:23:42,690 --> 00:23:45,030
Yes, right.

419
00:23:45,630 --> 00:23:47,960
I checked if she had any porridge...

420
00:23:48,570 --> 00:23:51,070
and brought back
the side-dish containers.

421
00:23:52,770 --> 00:23:54,640
Give them to me.
I will put them away.

422
00:23:54,740 --> 00:23:55,970
No, it is fine.

423
00:23:56,510 --> 00:23:59,210
I will put them away,
so do not worry...

424
00:23:59,280 --> 00:24:01,240
and head inside
to open the restaurant.

425
00:24:16,260 --> 00:24:17,290
Mother.

426
00:24:42,990 --> 00:24:46,090
One person makes the mess,
and another cleans it up.

427
00:24:47,690 --> 00:24:48,790
Pardon? What did you say?

428
00:24:50,290 --> 00:24:53,460
It is nothing.
I will finish cleaning up.

429
00:24:58,370 --> 00:25:01,170
This must be how Mom felt
whenever she cleaned my room.

430
00:25:04,140 --> 00:25:05,180
Ms. Kang Da Mi.

431
00:25:06,410 --> 00:25:07,410
Yes?

432
00:25:09,650 --> 00:25:11,150
I am going to give you
an assignment.

433
00:25:12,280 --> 00:25:13,450
Sure, what is it?

434
00:25:19,320 --> 00:25:20,720
These three outfits...

435
00:25:20,790 --> 00:25:22,730
are from this year's
Hwanggeum Hotel spring summer line.

436
00:25:23,230 --> 00:25:25,030
Yes, and?

437
00:25:25,530 --> 00:25:27,560
They all suffered poor sales.

438
00:25:28,060 --> 00:25:29,330
And from what I see,

439
00:25:29,400 --> 00:25:30,600
the pieces for the first half
of next year...

440
00:25:30,670 --> 00:25:32,770
do not look significantly different
from this line.

441
00:25:33,100 --> 00:25:35,440
I want you to find out...

442
00:25:35,440 --> 00:25:39,510
why these outfits sold so poorly
and report back to me.

443
00:25:39,880 --> 00:25:42,080
By when?

444
00:25:43,580 --> 00:25:47,980
Would 2 days be enough?
I will give you 48 hours.

445
00:25:51,190 --> 00:25:52,190
What is the matter?

446
00:25:52,960 --> 00:25:56,630
Well, I just became an assistant,

447
00:25:56,930 --> 00:25:59,800
so I am a bit taken aback
that you are giving me...

448
00:26:00,130 --> 00:26:01,830
such a huge assignment.

449
00:26:03,500 --> 00:26:04,530
Do you plan to remain
an assistant...

450
00:26:04,600 --> 00:26:05,940
for the rest of your life?

451
00:26:06,540 --> 00:26:08,200
Isn't your goal
to become a designer?

452
00:26:08,370 --> 00:26:10,610
That is true, but...

453
00:26:13,710 --> 00:26:15,250
You do not look confident at all.

454
00:26:16,450 --> 00:26:18,680
If you cannot find a proper answer,

455
00:26:20,080 --> 00:26:21,790
do not bother coming
to the office tomorrow.

456
00:26:22,350 --> 00:26:23,620
I said two days.

457
00:26:24,220 --> 00:26:25,220
That is 48 hours.

458
00:26:26,220 --> 00:26:29,360
Wait, don't bother coming in?

459
00:26:30,660 --> 00:26:31,860
Yes. Is there a problem?

460
00:26:33,030 --> 00:26:36,730
You were the one who first...

461
00:26:36,800 --> 00:26:39,170
asked me to work as your assistant.

462
00:26:39,940 --> 00:26:42,340
I gave it a lot of thought
and took it.

463
00:26:42,510 --> 00:26:43,670
And now, for my first real task,

464
00:26:43,740 --> 00:26:46,010
you dump something on me
that I cannot handle.

465
00:26:47,040 --> 00:26:49,210
How am I supposed to do it properly?

466
00:26:49,810 --> 00:26:52,680
So you are saying
you lack confidence?

467
00:26:53,980 --> 00:26:55,850
Yes, honestly, I do.

468
00:27:00,390 --> 00:27:01,420
Ms. Kang Da Mi.

469
00:27:02,290 --> 00:27:04,790
- Yes?
- Why draw the line yourself...

470
00:27:04,860 --> 00:27:07,760
and say you can't handle it
without even trying?

471
00:27:09,030 --> 00:27:11,700
Working as my assistant,
you'll constantly be overwhelmed...

472
00:27:11,870 --> 00:27:13,270
with things you think
you can't handle.

473
00:27:17,270 --> 00:27:18,610
I guess I misjudged you.

474
00:27:19,440 --> 00:27:20,440
You can leave now.

475
00:27:23,680 --> 00:27:25,250
Leave?

476
00:27:26,620 --> 00:27:28,280
Are you firing me right now?

477
00:27:42,800 --> 00:27:44,670
(Mission: Mompossible)

478
00:28:00,880 --> 00:28:03,090
You already knew,
didn't you, Mrs. Choi?

479
00:28:03,350 --> 00:28:04,920
About my brother-in-law
and that woman's family.

480
00:28:05,020 --> 00:28:06,660
They moved to this neighborhood.

481
00:28:06,990 --> 00:28:08,990
You told me Mother asked Dr. Ju...

482
00:28:09,130 --> 00:28:11,260
to do a private job to find someone.

483
00:28:11,460 --> 00:28:15,030
- Jeon Jin Sook, was it?
- She still remembers that?

484
00:28:15,270 --> 00:28:17,630
Watching you for one day
and telling you not to come back...

485
00:28:17,700 --> 00:28:19,300
couldn't it be a test?

486
00:28:19,300 --> 00:28:21,140
Even if you do get fired,

487
00:28:21,140 --> 00:28:23,540
wouldn't it be better
to at least ask for the real reason?

488
00:28:24,010 --> 00:28:26,010
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
